! SINRAYTRA: one real ray and the matching paraxial ray (OpticStudio's
! Single Ray Trace).  f/2.5 singlet at 10 deg, C d F.
LEN NEW
TIT 'OSDsinglet'
EPD 20
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -32.4637
PIM
YAN 0 7 10
WL 656.27 587.56 486.13
! defaults: Hy 1, Py 1 (upper marginal ray, full field), reference wavelength
SINRAYTRA ; GO
! a near-axis ray agrees with the paraxial one (the paraxial ray starts at
! the real ray's object point), also at another wavelength; tangents
SINRAYTRA ; HX 0 ; HY 0.001 ; PX 0.001 ; PY 0 ; COO TAN ; GO
SINRAYTRA ; HY 0.001 ; PY 0.001 ; SETWV 3 ; COO TAN ; GO
! skew ray at the blue wavelength; the paraxial table compares with PXTY/PXTX
SINRAYTRA ; HX 0.5 ; HY 0.5 ; PX 0.7 ; PY -0.7 ; SETWV 3 ; GO
SINRAYTRA ; HX 0 ; HY 1 ; PX 0 ; PY 1 ; COO TAN ; GO
PXTY ALL
! a concave mirror: the direction cosines turn back (N < 0)
LEN NEW
EPD 20
YAN 0 1
RDY S1 -100
RMD S1 REFL
PIM
SINRAYTRA ; HY 1 ; PY 0.5 ; GO
! bad input
HX 0.5
SINRAYTRA ; HX 2 ; COO SIDEWAYS ; GO
